text:
maria: Quick heads-up — the streaming sample app is failing on slow links. Clients intermittently throw a parse error and then spawn reconnect storms.

jasper: Seen it locally. Repro steps: run the sample behind a throttled link (50kb/s) + long-lived SSE stream. After ~30s, client prints 400-ish parse errors.

aaron: Logs from the browser show the EventSource onmessage handler receives '\n' or ':' comment lines as payload and we call JSON.parse on them. Crash.

sophie: That sounds like heartbeat/comments per SSE spec getting treated as messages. Server sends periodic comment heartbeats like `:
` to keep proxies alive. Browser EventSource should ignore comment lines, but our SDK's polyfill parser doesn't.

maria: Repro log excerpt: ```
[client] chunk received: ":\n"
[client] chunk received: "data: {\"t\":\"tok\"}\n\n"
[client] parse error: Unexpected token ":" in JSON at position 0
```

jasper: Also noticed chunk boundary splits — sometimes the comment line and following data line get coalesced in a single read (proxy flush) so parser sees `:
data: {...}` as one chunk and mistakes it.

aaron: Two separate issues: 1) polyfill treating comment lines as messages, 2) parser not tolerant of empty data or leading comment chars. Node SDK behavior differs (it strips comment lines) -> parity bug.

sophie: Proposed SDK fix: update streaming parser to drop any event where `data` is empty after trimming, and strip leading `:` comment-only lines before handing to JSON.parse. Also add a safe-parse helper that returns null for empty input instead of throwing.

maria: Minimal server-side mitigation for sample app: change heartbeat to send `:

` (a proper SSE comment) and ensure we flush on its own line. But we still need client fix.

aaron: Patch idea (JS): ```js
// in stream parser
function parseEventChunk(chunk) {
  // drop comment-only events (lines starting with ':')
  if (/^:\s*$/m.test(chunk)) return null;
  const dataLine = chunk.split(/?
/).filter(Boolean).find(l => l.startsWith('data:')) || '';
  const payload = dataLine.replace(/^data:\s*/, '');
  if (!payload.trim()) return null;
  try {
    return JSON.parse(payload);
  } catch (e) {
    // non-fatal: emit parse_debug metric and ignore
    metrics.increment('stream.parse_errors');
    return null;
  }
}
```

jasper: We should also add test cases: interleaved `:
` comment + partial `data:` chunk boundaries, and ensure Node/browser parity.

sophie: For immediate protection on Hosted we can patch the polyfill and roll a minor SDK release. Low risk. I'll open PR with tests.

maria: Created issue #3421 and linked to the sample-app repo. Repro steps and curl command: `curl -N -H "Accept: text/event-stream" https://local/sample-stream | sed -n '1,200p'`

deploy-bot: deploy job queued for branch `devex/sse-fix` (CI: queued) :hourglass_flowing_sand: 

aaron: Also found one quirky case: proxies that concatenate small writes can produce `:
data` in a single packet — parser must tolerate leading `:` tokens then data.

maria: Action items: 
• sophie: PR to SDK parser + tests (owner)
• jasper: add Node/browser parity e2e in sample-app (owner)
• aaron: add metric `stream.parse_errors` + alert if >100/min
• maria: temporary note in onboarding doc about throttled networks + workaround

sophie: I'll try to get the PR out today and ship a 0.4.1 patch if CI is green.

jasper: Thanks — if anyone hits it in prod, add `?force=no-heartbeat` flag to the sample app (will disable server comments) until SDK drop. :thumbsup: 

maria: Cool. I'll follow up in #product-infra with a short blurb for the SDK changelog.
